-- Row il-79. EXPECTED RED: four assertions that fail on purpose. Three are for I1, each scoped to the rows one table prints, and the fourth is for I2.
-- R1 (I1): 19 appears under the heading for the new section in the rows the row types from the table of SH 1123 under the sub-heading for the 1957 Law. It fails: 19 appears under the heading for the previous section, with 41 beside it.
-- R2 (I1): 8 appears under the heading for the new section in the table of NV 19. It fails: 8 appears under the heading for the previous section, with 12 beside it.
-- R3 (I1): 12 appears under the heading for the new section in the rows the row types from the table of SH 1123 under the sub-heading for the 1971 new version. It fails: 12 appears under the heading for the previous section, with 96 beside it.
-- R4 (I2): some instruction of SH 2760, the instrument that prints the definition of "the court" in place of the one in section 1, names section 38 of the Law. It fails: SH 2760 prints three sections, on section 1 of the Law, on a section of the Courts Law and on application, and none names section 38.
-- The assertions are about the position of a number in a printed table, and about what an instrument's sections name; the row says nothing about what a table means. The count, four, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red).

